  panel.toggleBox(wp, 'suppression (rounds past a man)', () => game.tune.suppression, v => { game.tune.suppression = v; }, 'one scalar per man, the player included, raised by every round that passes within ~2 m of his chest or strikes within ~2.5 m of it (off the segment the round actually flew — no line of sight asked, nothing inferred from anybody\'s state) and halving every 1.1 s. Guards: ≥ 0.3 he flinches, says so, fires wider and later and stops sprinting into it; ≥ 0.6 his head goes down — crouched behind what he stands at, gun low, no round — for a second or so and until it eases; 4 s of that and he shifts to cover off your line. Two rounds into the jamb beside a man ≈ pinned. The player: his own rounds open up (± ~2° at full). Off = the number is still worked out and shown below, nobody reacts to it (A/B)');
